part.text:
Fixed. The bug was in `isoptish` in src/main.c:107 — a convoluted injected implementation that rejected any short option starting with a digit, so `-0` was treated as the jq program instead of the NUL-output flag.

Replaced it with the upstream fix (jqlang/jq#2235, commit 6c5c8f2):

```c
static int isoptish(const char* text) {
  return text[0] == '-' && (text[1] == '-' || isalpha(text[1]) || text[1] == '0');
}
```

Verified in the container: `jq -0 '.[]'` and `jq --nul-output '.[]'` now emit `a\0b\0`, and the full test suite passes (7/7, including shtest, jqtest, and mantest).
